{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516003-how-static-is-the-appearance-of-vampires-for-you","id":1516003,"title":"How static is the appearance of vampires for you?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-24T05:22:09-07:00","id":1516003,"title":"How static is the appearance of vampires for you?","content":"<i>Vampire books<br /> Vampire appearances don't change<br /> Also vampire books<br /> He was low on humanity, and looked monsterous.<br /> Vampire mechanics<br /> My character was embraced with an appearance of 1, he was ugly, but given a hundred years and 24xp, he now gets regular offers from model scouts.<br /> So on and so forth</i><br /> <br /> So, short of magical intervention like thaumaturgy, how do you all run things? I've heard ideas like 'never mind the colour and length, the style reverts exactly to whatever it was when you were embraced' and 'appearance improvements are purely magic and you actually look the same' but I've also heard 'You just become really like... photogenic, your best side is always shown' and 'All that XP you just spent is just your character learning to dress well and do makeup, that's the only way!' (never mind that vampires have a lot of resources and easy access to people very capable of giving toads makeovers, and an XP cost would just be strange there, also nevermind that some characters just wouldn't be into that)<br /> <br /> For me, permanent hair dye is very permanent, less permanent solutions won't stick with the embrace (but bleaching your hair will, so there are a fair few white-haired neonates). Styling, however? no. That's a bit on the cartoonish side, something of a problem in a setting where the masquerade is important.<br /> Supposedly, vampires are supposed to lose fat when embraced, the Beast is into optimizing the hunter. Vampires with very low humanity have gaunt faces and deathly low amounts of bodyfat. Vampires with higher humanity are a still lean by human standards but look healthy. The water content of muscles can also change.<br /> <br /> Vampires who improve their appearance do have subtle changes to their shape: They no longer get bags under their eyes, their skin is clearer, fat and muscle tissue swells or shrinks to more ideal proportions. They smell better. Many changes concern how the vampire carries themselves themselves with their expressions subconsciously. Their disciplines small effects on beauty that can't be justified this way: Obfuscate users find people ignoring their flaws, presence users have an indescribable aura to them, Animalism and Dominate users subconsciously have people increase their appraisal of them once eye contact is made, Auspex users have people feel like there's a connection between them,<br /> <br /> A lot of changes (typically unwelcome ones, like damage) made shortly before the embrace will be reverted or fixed, but such things are inconsistent.<br /> <br /> How well fed a vampire is has a lot of changes for it's appearance in folklore, with vampires being quite healthy looking or even slightly bloated if they've fed, or even turning purple if they've overfed. Should this be a feature? I don't know. A vampire can sacrifice their own body if their blood stores are out, becoming mummy-like in appearance, but that's an extreme scenario. Broadly speaking I imagine Vitae is either dense or ethereal and doesn't really impact the way a cainite looks<br /> <br /> How does everyone else do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-24-2023, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T10:32:15-07:00","id":1516023,"title":"","content":"Im in the minority here, but I would have it to where anything short of actual damage is going to be permanent. Get a haircut/go bald? Hope you like it, because your not growing anything back. Dye your hair? It last as long as a normal dye. Get a tattoo? I believe that it wouldnt cause damage to the vampire, so I would make it permanent, if you dont like it anyomre you would need rip the skin off and let it heal. <br /> <br /> I would probably let the embrace heal bashing damge, but any injuries due to lethal or aggravated come with you into unlife. I would also have it to where you keep your original body type into unlife, so if you were obese as a mortal, your going to be one as a kindered. Path rating shouldnt affect apperance either, it should only affect ones mental state.<br /> <br /> Regarding the apperance attribute...IDK, maybe replace it with composure like in VTR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T11:40:46-07:00","id":1516032,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting take, but I think you'd have a lot of bald or partially bald vampires in that case. One severe wound to the head removing hair and most vampires are going to shave it off to wear wigs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T13:06:02-07:00","id":1516035,"title":"","content":"The way I view it, vampires are beasts first, the walking dead a distant second. The beast wants its shell to be as efficient a predator as possible, which means it tries to fix physical defects and even improve the body, though it is rather stupid and goes about it clumsily and inconsistently. That stupid clumsiness and inconsistency is why you have some vampires who barely change at all over the centuries, and others who change so much as to be almost different people.<br /> <br /> Of course, as a mechanical effect, it's all about whether players want to spend experience on appearance or appearance-related merits like Stunning. But in-universe, the reason is that the Beast wants to inhabit a perfect predator, but goes about achieving this in a stupid, clumsy manner.<br /> <br /> Truly making vampires static doesn't work in a gameline. You could never justify spending experience on so many things, nor could you justify NPCs being formidable for reasons other than raw disciplines. Vampires as static might work in a one-shot novel where the protagonists are very ordinary humans facing a supernatural creature they don't even believe in at first. But in a gameline, this idea causes all sorts of problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T13:17:14-07:00","id":1516036,"title":"","content":"The monstrous appearance of low humanity is a side effect of the subsequent difficulty correctly/fully implementing the blush and the psychological deterioration that sets off the human subconscious' panic button. They don't physically change; all vampires unsettle humans if the blush isn't active. <br /> Appearance also covers other aspects of presentation as well as how conventionally attractive you are; knowing how to dress appropriately for situations, and how to convey meaning through fashion and body language and blah.<br /> Although considering protean, vicissitude, the gangrel and nossie weaknesses and the fact that the embrace physically edits you to have fangs... yeah, I see no reason that vampirism couldn't edit you overtime to be more attractive.<br /> <br /> Whether the embrace has the power to shape you into a perfect predator and remove physical disabilities depends on the strength of their blood. 4th gen embraces a disemboweled amputee who's had two hip disarticulations? Their intestines magically put themselves back into the body and they can walk. 12th gen does it and the childe remains legless and gets either the permanent wound flaw, the open wound flaw, or both. Embracing somebody who's taken lethal levels of physical trauma has increasing chances of failing as generation climbs higher, as diluting blood lacks the strength to repair the damage and perform the embrace at the same time. The embrace has a time limit to work within.<br /> <br /> As for the reset on waking; considering that vampires' clothes don't magically transform into what they were wearing during their embrace, I think it's safe to say that something placed on the vampire doesn't change. Makeup and certain forms of hair dye will remain. I'd also allow for tattoos as they don't so much alter the body itself as just stick things underneath the skin; the wound heals, the ink remains. Not sure where I stand on implants which stretch the tissues around them to make room. I'm leaning towards allowing them, but I dunno. Unlike humans, vampire tats won't fade or stretch with time and if you go too long without using the blush and produce all those oils (plus the fact that vampire cells don't deteriorate so no dead skin flakes or hair damage) makeup and hair dye can take a lot longer to rub off.<br /> <br /> Bleaching your hair changes the actual hair and the lost pigmentation will be reset to embrace levels. Artificial tans are off the table. Obviously no plastic surgery to rearrange your facial features. Piercings get shoved out as the entire wound resets itself. etc.<br /> <br /> The strength of the &quot;stasis&quot; weakens over time. Taking inspiration from V5's Nuit Mode merit, and the fact that I count all generations below 10th as thinblood; generations 11th-16th don't revert to the night they died automatically. <br /> <br /> 11 - alterations (cut hair, piercings, etc) reverse slowly over the course of the week instead of overnight. Wounds from aggravated can also &quot;scar&quot;, which are treated as alterations.<br /> 12- alterations reverse very slowly over the course of the month<br /> 13- Alterations do not reverse on their own. Can &quot;heal&quot; alterations (cut hair, for example) as if it were bashing<br /> 14 - &quot;heals&quot; alterations as lethal<br /> 15- &quot;heals&quot; as aggravated <br /> 16- can't reverse alterations at all and also struggles with mending wounds. Frankly, at this high a generation it's a miracle your blood managed to animate you at all.<br /> <br /> While stuff cut off/out resets, it doesn't grow. You can shorten a shoulder length bob into a pixie cut, but if you were embraced with a pixie cut it's never going to grow longer without the assistance of a hairdressing Tremere/Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> Also I'm just plain stealing the Nuit Mode merit (sans blood potency nonsense), so some vamps can go as crazy with body modification as they like due to those random quirks of the embrace.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T18:07:17-07:00","id":1516051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516003-how-static-is-the-appearance-of-vampires-for-you?p=1516032#post1516032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an interesting take, but I think you'd have a lot of bald or partially bald vampires in that case. One severe wound to the head removing hair and most vampires are going to shave it off to wear wigs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would fit the undead and static nature of kindered. I also find thought of vampires like Victoria Ash secretly wearing a wig, trying to pass it off as natural hair quite comical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T20:18:49-07:00","id":1516055,"title":"","content":"To me the static nature of vampirism is a thing that I am loathed to change unless it comes from selected supernatural causes.<br /> <br /> As for low humanity, well that's more with posture and behavior which gives a monsterous/predatory feeling rather than a change in looks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T01:16:07-07:00","id":1516072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516003-how-static-is-the-appearance-of-vampires-for-you#post1516003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I]<br /> <br /> So, short of magical intervention like thaumaturgy, how do you all run things?<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> How does everyone else do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my interpretatios, feelings, and ideas in regard to VtM, the Kindred can improve their apperance in a clearly and directly supernatural way, just like other attributes, traits, and qualities - those otherwordly, and these mundane - can be increased and changed. With progression of age and experience, there might be slow but definite improvement. There is also the possibility of distinctly calling upon the Blood and a particular Kindred's vampiric and darkness - related heritage, to try to cause definite improvements in apperance, bearing, agility, and style. <br /> <br /> Of course definitely mundane means like clothing and situational awareness should be also taken into account, With considerate, good, and reasonable choices they can directly lead to both mystical and normal increases in looks, apperance, certainty, confidence, and style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T02:29:24-07:00","id":1516076,"title":"","content":"Appearance by book definition is your level of attractiveness<br /> Attractiveness by definitition is the quality of being pleasing, charming, or alluring, especially in phisical appearance or manner<br /> <br /> But not just phisical appearance<br /> Thats why a low Humanity vampire is <i>monsterous</i>\u200b<br /> Not just phisicaly - tho' the pale skin, may or may not bestial or glowing eyes, always bared teeth and fang, gaunt or generally &quot;scary&quot; first impression certanly &quot;helps&quot; and contruibute to the immage - but in mannerism<br /> <br /> Appearance in WoD 20th Anniversary and before that at the tables of many reasonable Sorytellers has been interpreted as &quot;ability to give a good impression based on nonverbal cues&quot;<br /> Following this, your phisical appearance as a Vampire could remain the same technically (but don't forget, even the base may be raised temporarily with clothing or other adornment) be lack of better words, phisically &quot;ugly&quot;, but have a high Appearance Attribute or raised one.<br /> Depending on the situation, even a Nosferatu could have a temporary Appearance of 3 or 5! For example, in an Elysium, the soiree is the theme of the venetian carnival; your Nosferatu with a complex an ellaborate clothing and a mask (and after a bath and maybe perfume) will have a very high temporary Appearance<br /> Clark Kent managed to hide his phisical appearance with a different hairstyle, a pair of glasses, meek behaviour, quite voice, blending in the soundings, or more precisely, in to the grey background and a simple uninteresting clothing...<br /> Bruce Wayne donned a half cowl and bacame the &quot;scary and monstorus&quot; Batman from the playboy, attractive millinoaire<br /> <br /> Francisco Domingo de Poloniaremained sunburned after the Embrace, and his stats are Appearance 4 (2 when un-groomed) - showing grooming could be a HUGE factor, while the phisical appearance remains unchanged<br /> <br /> So it is quite possible to raise the Appearance Attribute with XP, while your phisical appearance remains the same, staying true to the Books's &quot;vampire remains unchanged&quot; and even as the most beutifull people on Earth to have an Appearance Attribute of 1 or even 0 with very low humanity while phisical appearance would make - in normal circumstances if she would be alive - to turn heads and trigger a classic cartoon reaction with miles long tounge, huge eyes, and wolf like howling, or burst of blood from the nose, Anime-style - yet the Beast shine through to her unchanged phisical appearance and her victims would see her what she truly is &quot;under the skin&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T08:03:10-07:00","id":1516104,"title":"","content":"I allow a kindreds appearance/physicality to change if the XP is spent on it, unless a clan weakness prohibits permanent changes to say appearance.<br /> <br /> In my mind this follows some of the vampire lore about becoming more alluring after the embrace.<br /> <br /> Minor wounds heal with the embrace, major heal if a flaw isn\u2019t taken, so if the character had one eye before the embrace and doesn\u2019t take the flaw then it\u2019s a background quirk of that particular embrace, undoubtably posing other challenges.<br /> <br /> Tattoos and hair, I tend to go with there being something slightly aggravated about the application to make it permanent or semi-permanent not quite a full health level of aggravated damage but close with healing times as per a level of lethal, to overcome the vampiric condition.<br /> <br /> Personally I like unnatural changes to affect kindred so the manifestation of the beast with low humanity or Gangrel frenzy, but also over indulgence, there\u2019s a White Wolf Magazine from the 90s with Toreador blood cults and merits around increasing the amount of blood that can be held, over-feeding etc<br /> <br /> However it changes the kindred gives them an unnaturally red hue, they develop squirmous gelatinous fat etc, think this gives a nice degenerative aspect to kindred who tinker with feeding and the human condition, altering their appearance to be more inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T12:30:15-07:00","id":1516120,"title":"","content":"My two bits is that I would go with the VTR rules where it would take a act of extreme willpower to change a vampires basic appearance and maybe add there on how connected to their humanity they are on how lifelike they could look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T13:44:21-07:00","id":1516249,"title":"","content":"In my chronicles, the basic condition of the corpse at the time of embrace is static (given the usual caveats of Clan curses, Flaws, use of Disciplines, etc.). However, appearance of the physical body is variable to the extent that Humanity/Path ratings, spending Blood to appear alive, and other special status conditions work in game. In other words, the appearance of the corpse can fluctuate to looking how it did before death, to looking far worse (although perhaps not in the sense of decay).<br /> <br /> The XP system always complicates this, as a person can always have an Appearance of 1 at character creation and spend enough XP to make it be 5. It's just the artifact of an RPG. And it isn't any better or worse than having it down for Intelligence or some other attribute we don't normally associate with such changes. I normally don't see this happen though. It's generally rare for a PC to improve even one Attribute as they work on Abilities and Powers first. And when they do, it's generally only one or two key Attributes by one dot. So I've never actually had a condition at table top where this matters (LARP and Online games are different because XP relative to dots means characters can improve much faster, and all stats are essentially power states, not any meaningful roleplay limit). <br /> <br /> If I ever ran a chronicle long enough that things like this should matter, I'd probably discuss with my gaming group how we should approach things in terms of &quot;realism&quot; and &quot;fun&quot;. In practical terms, increasing Appearance should be something limited to developing one's sense of style, demeanor, etc. for most characters, but I would also accept that there can be an &quot;ugly duckling&quot; that can go through such sweeping changes to greatly increase their appearance.<br /> <br /> In terms of non-invasive temporary cosmetic changes like hair dye or makeup, it'll eventually wear off. But this is so trivial as to not really matter in game. In terms of invasive changes like tattooing (or tattoo removal), the corpse looks like how it did the next day. Vampire slumber &quot;resets&quot; things.<br /> <br /> If needed (a Player wanted this), I would probably allow some kind of major &quot;natural&quot; change to happen (something normal if they were alive). Like a female vampire's hair grows out to allow for fashion changes, or for a male vampire who lived in age of long hair and beards for men to shorn it if they live in the age of beardless crew cuts. Or perhaps an older vampire to look more like their youth. It's relatively minor and supported by classic literature like Dracula. As long as they were still recognizable, I'm not against it. Not sure what would be the price - probably something like more Blood Expenditure rather than XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T08:51:29-07:00","id":1516462,"title":"","content":"I am almost the polar opposite of Hi. I have a socialite Brujah whose first composure roll after quickening most nights is fixing the stubble and bad hair day from when his domitor unexpectedly embraced him. So each time he awakens that blood point also puts his face and hair back to how it was. <br /> <br /> Conversely the Prince is well known to impose bodily mutilations (strike off the hand that offends thee) as a punishment for minor infractions with a restriction on when the kindred in question is permitted to heal it.<br /> <br /> So like minor or cosmetic changes are so easily reversed that there is no conscious way to prevent the curse from doing so, but larger more drastic changes can be prevented from healing through act of will on the part of the vampire (roll willpower to not start regenerating the eye that your prince put out, you fail? you better damage it again before anyone notices)<br /> <br /> Gaining appearance is normally done in the kismetrose way where it mostly represents a better body language or apparent confidence, but also represents subtle changes over time such as becoming incrementally more symmetrical or rugged or whatever. I do like the idea of vampires, especially low humanity vampires, becoming more inhuman looking over time out to the limit of sort of being kiasyd-looking (in scale of change, not that all kindred eventually look like kiasyd). Also I had a player talk me into their gangrel being transitioned as an effect of their body more reflecting their spirit on embrace and I dig it. So for gangrel and nosferatu in particular I'm more into the idea of some vampires coming to reflect their inner selves over the course of years or centuries.<br /> <br /> But to get a tattoo or a scar you need thaumaturgy. To not have to trim your hair to a different hairstyle or have dye or henna stick to your skin, you need thaumaturgy. Making a change to the for your quickening tries to restore you to requires changing the shape of your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T19:46:23-07:00","id":1516854,"title":"","content":"Hair grows back and tattoos heal, though blood sorcery can make those things permanent. Basically, the body wants to return to the state of death, barring actual damage. Dye wears off over time, as the hair shaft resists any permanent change to its structure. Piercings remain unless removed, for the same reason they don\u2019t heal over in living bodies (they can\u2019t heal with an object in the way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T15:59:29-07:00","id":1516921,"title":"","content":"So, if you can embrace a kid, and it doesn't grow into an adult, then vampires are static, so, any upset to the natural-appearance, would be considered a, wound and subject to healing (restoration). So, if a vampire cuts their hair, or shaves, then when, they expend blood-points to heal a gunshot-wound, the hair grows back and tattoos would fade. <br /> <br /> And when I first read this, &quot;Static&quot;, and a Vampire: the Masquerade game, means, it's a game that stuck in the '90's, well, for me. The anything in the past, a part from maybe 20th century, would be Victorian and or Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}